<metadata><name>Day 21 (stop 2 of 2) - Beeney Creek, Sixth Line, Sixth Line trailhead</name></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.658281" lon="-79.985371"><name>P Start/finish parking</name><desc>Where the main Trail exits the forest on the west side of Sixth Line. Free</desc><sym>Parking Area</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.662210" lon="-79.990410"><name>P2 alternative parking</name><desc>Sixth Line parking (south), new July 2026 for the Silver Creek trail changes (BTC notice…. Fee unclear. Joins the route near km 0.0 (800 m walk).</desc><sym>Parking Area</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.648060" lon="-79.995230"><name>P3 alternative parking</name><desc>Fifth Line parking at the Beeney Creek Side Trail (new June 2025, BTC Map 12; location traced…. Fee unclear. Joins the route near km 1.5 (0 m walk).</desc><sym>Parking Area</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.658435" lon="-79.985636"><name>J1</name><desc>J1: Turn left onto the blue-blazed Sixth Line Side Trail, heading south-west.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.655368" lon="-79.988987"><name>J2</name><desc>J2: Continue straight onto the white-blazed main Bruce Trail, heading south-west. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off on your left.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.653565" lon="-79.990790"><name>J3</name><desc>J3: Continue straight onto the blue-blazed Beeney Creek Side Trail, heading south-west. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off on your right.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.648057" lon="-79.995235"><name>J4</name><desc>J4: Turnaround point. There is trailhead parking here (Fifth Line parking at the Beeney Creek Side Trail (new June 2025, BTC Map 12; location…). Turn around and retrace your steps.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
